{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"color","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLElisionV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision\/color"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision\/color"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLElision"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLElision"}],"title":"MXLElision","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The elision type represents an elision between lyric syllables. The text content specifies the symbol used to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display the elision. Common values are a no-break space (Unicode 00A0), an underscore (Unicode 005F), or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"undertie (Unicode 203F). If the text content is empty, the smufl attribute is used to specify the symbol to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use. Its value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics. The SMuFL attribute is ignored if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elision glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor a smufl attribute are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present, the elision glyph is application-specific."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision/color":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision\/color","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision\/color","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"title":"color","kind":"symbol"}}}